# Who GitHub asks to review every pull request (never its author). It asks them itself, so each
# request shows as coming from the pull request's author: no workflow or token is involved.
#
# The ruleset only needs one approving review from someone with write access, and that review
# comes from @princesseke: GitHub never lets authors approve their own pull requests, so the
# owners, @gigabytedevelopersinc and @enwokoma, cannot approve theirs. She is listed here so that
# she is asked on every pull request, including those touching only the paths below.
#
# Entries have to be user accounts or @org/team names with write access. The organisation itself
# (@gigabytedevelopers) is neither, which is why this file once matched nobody and no review was
# ever requested automatically.
*       @gigabytedevelopersinc @enwokoma @princesseke

# The release machinery and anything that touches signing deserves a second look. The last
# matching line wins, so each one names everyone again.
/.github/                   @gigabytedevelopersinc @enwokoma @princesseke
/app/build.gradle           @gigabytedevelopersinc @enwokoma @princesseke
/cliff.toml                 @gigabytedevelopersinc @enwokoma @princesseke
